# The build context is sent to the daemon on every build, and anything that
# lands in it can end up in a layer. Both halves of that matter here.

# Host-installed dependencies and build output. A better-sqlite3 binding
# compiled on the host will not load inside the image; the build makes its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite

# The database. Copied into a layer it would ship as if it were the
# deployment's own data, and the volume that should hold it would sit empty.
data
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm

# Secrets belong to the platform, never to an image anyone can pull and read.
.env
.env.*

.git
.gitignore
.github
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Not needed to build or to run the server.
server/tests
docs
README.md
fly.toml
render.yaml
